rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5617456Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5627487Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5726800Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5736598Z ^[[0m
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5737388Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5738390Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5738836Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5739240Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5740401Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5740982Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5741351Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5742104Z    if you are ready to continue.
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5742473Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5743129Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5744570Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5745497Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5746253Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5746591Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5746987Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5747528Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5747946Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5748705Z    can use Nix.
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5748982Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5749201Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5749549Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5751913Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5752895Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5753310Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5753487Z I will:
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5753750Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5753991Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5754488Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5754985Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5755427Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5755740Z  - install Nix in /nix
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5756053Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5756503Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5756924Z    /root
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5767416Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5768120Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5779065Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5779800Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5780522Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5781445Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5782158Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5799699Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5800616Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5811112Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5811963Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5812425Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5813175Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5813445Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5813711Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5813959Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5815057Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5815480Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5815680Z If you would like to
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5816161Z see the output, try like this:
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5816513Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5816754Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5817184Z   $ sh ./install-nix
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5817350Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5817361Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5817624Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:51.5824009Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
