rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6095273Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6101748Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6177626Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6184902Z ^[[0m
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6185208Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6185817Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6186025Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6186260Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6186770Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6187088Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6187286Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6187666Z    if you are ready to continue.
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6187847Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6188200Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6189168Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6189608Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6189944Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6190121Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6190288Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6190531Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6190730Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6191088Z    can use Nix.
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6191220Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6191325Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6191478Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6197172Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6198128Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6198389Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6198516Z I will:
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6198760Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6198920Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6199176Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6199442Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6199686Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6199869Z  - install Nix in /nix
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6200062Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6200318Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6200546Z    /root
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6277729Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6278145Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6286882Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6287219Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6287396Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6288689Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6289035Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6303139Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6303565Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6311618Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6312142Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6312426Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6312794Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6312928Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6313153Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6313338Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6313711Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6314027Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6314130Z If you would like to
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6314382Z see the output, try like this:
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6314548Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6314724Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6315167Z   $ sh ./install-nix
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6315349Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6315368Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6315654Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.6322101Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
