rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2125755Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2134278Z ^[[0m
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2134735Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2135270Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2135518Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2135672Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2136048Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2136286Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2136424Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2136709Z    if you are ready to continue.
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2136848Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2137112Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2138361Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2138886Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2139283Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2139489Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2139688Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2139985Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2140217Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2140677Z    can use Nix.
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2140994Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2141071Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2141213Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2141430Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2141778Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2145073Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2145184Z I will:
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2145485Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2145831Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2146316Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2146809Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2147266Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2147843Z  - install Nix in /nix
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2148149Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2148612Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2149083Z    /root
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2213306Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2214051Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2223737Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2224222Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2224521Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2225907Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2226395Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2246410Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2247284Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2257617Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2258273Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2258721Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2259349Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2259542Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T09:37:48.2259810Z 
